 fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\n- [ ] Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n- [ ] A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\n- [ ] Lint clean\n- [ ] Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\n- [ ] New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\n- [ ] Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\n\n## Task\n\n- **ID:** BUG-260916-1rqn1c\n- **Title:** BUG-260916-1rqn1c: align-ci-native-xcode-toolchain\n- **Parent:** STORY-260916-19w99a\n\n### Description\n\nPR6 head d45c85d67b78b6578b5cb0821bd2e78217124d30 hosted run35091586150 passes macOS target builds, Swift tests and release build, then native packaging rejects Xcode16.4 build16F6 because NativeDependencies manifest pins17F42. Determine and implement smallest supported toolchain alignment preserving artifact provenance and strict validation.\n\n### Scope\n\nHosted workflow and directly necessary native toolchain compatibility contracts; no unrelated product fixes, no VPN activation, no weakened checks\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\nA narrow reproducible fix has independent review, exact prospective PR composition identity, targeted validation and honest hosted validation requirements handed to parent; real hosted CI publication and landing are separate parent delivery obligations.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### BUG-260916-1rqn1c_implementation-brief.md\n> Narrow producer scope and exact prerequisite authorization\n\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.temp/resources/BUG-260916-1rqn1c/BUG-260916-1rqn1c_implementation-brief.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2670`\n- Content digest: `sha256:d5b8ad8b2ab110486c6611f028911ae2fcdd908ace82690f7e1a1299d9637dad`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### BUG-260916-1rqn1c_review-brief.md\n> Independent narrow source review routing\n\n# Independent source review\n\nAstra low reviewer, one worker. Read current CR, installed skill, producer outcome and official toolchain evidence. Review exact candidate against PR6 d45c85d67b78b6578b5cb0821bd2e78217124d30; candidate includes authorized 59-path prerequisite overlay from that head, not new product scope. Verify every prerequisite byte, isolate four proposed new paths, compute exact prospective PR tree preserving all board and remaining PR entries. Do not publish entire old-main candidate.\n\nAssess correctness and proportionality of macos-26 plus explicit17F42 selection, official documented app path/availability and architecture/Mise checksum pairing; strict rejection and artifact provenance must remain. Verify selection effects are limited to hosted job; no global xcode-select changes on this workstation. Check tests actually protect production behavior and how they are included in ongoing CI/gates; report unwired tests or source-string-only limits honestly. No fake hosted success: this source review can accept a valid local candidate pending separate publication/real hosted green. Inspect true exit-code evidence; producer initially piped commands to tail and was asked to preserve actual statuses. Reuse completed exact candidate full CR gate if valid, avoid redundant exhaustive suites.\n\nIndependently run meaningful focused tests and required review gates, check negative/mutant evidence and report coverage honestly (manual process identity evidence is not an executable test). Verify no manifest/artifact/product/deployment-target changes. If defects exist, request changes with concrete minimal fixes; do not implement. If accepted use actual accept_cr and attach task-scoped verdict, candidate identity, prospective composition tree and bounds. No commits, publication, rootLOGBOOK writes, tooling changes, nested workers, VPN or route mutation. Parent owns exact signed-head GitHub review and landing after hosted checks.\n\n\n### BUG-260916-1rqn1c_review-rev2-addendum.md\n> Review actual revised five-path candidate\n\nRev2 supersedes the four-path count in the original review brief: scripts/tests/test-credential-free-validation.sh is a fifth path with macos26 expectation and new regression/mutant suite wiring. Recovery RUN-260916-07614a proves full credential-free gate exit0, native gate exit0, incompatible17F113 exit1. Automatic immutable CR gate is separately rerunning. Read results-rev2.md and current CR, not only rev1. Main failure cause was hardcoded macos15 contract; mise trust issue was metadata noise, not actual exit1 cause. Preserve this distinction. Reviewer must compute exact prospective PR composition tree for all five paths and check any new bounds.\n\n\n### BUG-260916-1rqn1c_rework-rev2-brief.md\n> Fix concrete independent review findings only\n\nMuse max rework: read review-verdict-rev2.md completely enough for both findings. Fix new selector exact-build matching (17F420 must fail), add named negative and suffix-only narrowing mutant; fix workflow execution coverage with token-preserving echo-bypass mutant and genuinely executable command/effect test or strict executable-command contract. Supply narrowing mutants for new refusal gates called out by reviewer. Keep five-path scope, manifest/artifacts/product/deployment-target untouched, prerequisite59 bytes intact. Existing legacy libssh2 substring behavior is pre-existing and outside this slice. Correct coverage to executable vs manual evidence as reviewer2of6, do not count prose/tree identity as tests. Existing task-local mise trust is already resolved; do not redo unrelated setup. No globalxcode-select, VPN, nestedworkers, commits/publication/rootLOGBOOK writes. Run focused suite and contract lane; handoff automatic fullCRgate owns exhaustive validation, avoid redundant manual full run unless actual changes/failure justify it. Preserve exact candidate source for newCR; reviewer must accept before publication. Report failure causes truthfully and compute candidate/prospective identities or leave explicit to reviewer.\n\n\n\n\n## Evidence and Safety\n\n- Add/update a task-scoped outcome named `BUG-260916-1rqn1c_*` before handoff:\n  `task-board m 'add_resource(BUG-260916-1rqn1c, name=BUG-260916-1rqn1c_results.md, content=\"...\", type=outcome, description=\"Handoff evidence\")'`\n- Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior ships with negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; prove the bound by narrowing it, not only by deleting it, and name the production call site. Shapes and incidents: `references/negative-evidence.md`.\n- An absence and a failure to read are different facts; report unknown instead of inferring a property from a proxy signal.\n- Stop-The-Line only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only product/platform/architecture/approval decision. Persist evidence, failed attempts, options/tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact input needed; otherwise rework autonomously.\n- `to-review` is a role handoff, not accepted completion. Report **ready for review** or **handed off to review**.\n\n## LAST — Run For Role Handoff\n\nAfter AC, checklist, validation, and outcome evidence:\n\n```bash\ntask-board handoff BUG-260916-1rqn1c --role developer\n```\n\n## Working Directory\nBoard directory: `/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.task-board`\n\nWork in the project root. Never edit board files directly.\n\n## Story Workspace\n\nYou are running in an isolated Git worktree for STORY-260916-19w99a.\n\n- Workspace path: `.temp/STORY-260916-19w99a/worktree` (this is your working directory)\n- Branch: